 KDE's settings modules are shown inside it where Wild OS has no page of its
 own yet.
 .
 Its keyboard, printer, account, language and app permission pages work
 through kxkbrc and KWin, CUPS, AccountsService and two small root helpers,
 the regional settings KDE uses and Flatpak's override files. Its
 touchscreen, pen, game controller, AutoPlay and Thunderbolt pages use
 KWin, SDL, Plasma's device automounter and boltd. Spell checking goes
 through Sonnet, and fonts are installed for the account with fontconfig.
 File search and activity history use Baloo's and the activity manager's
 own settings.
 .
 Its accessibility page keeps every choice where KDE and KWin read it, and
 wildos-access gives high contrast, the on-screen keyboard and sticky keys
 their keyboard shortcuts in the session and on the lock and sign-in
 screens. Mono audio is a PipeWire filter run as a user service.
 .
 It also points the desktop's right-click "Personalise" entry at Settings
 and installs the small helper that sets automatic security updates.
 .
 Advanced network settings work through NetworkManager. The wildos-network
 service gives each new network Quad9's encrypted DNS (DNS over TLS through
 systemd-resolved) and runs the VPN kill switch with nftables; Wi-Fi uses a
 private hardware address for each network by default.
 .
 The firewall is one nftables table that settings-firewall builds from the
 protection level and the choices on the Firewall page, loaded again by
 wildos-network as networks come and go. File sharing, Remote Desktop and
 SSH install Samba, KRdp or OpenSSH the first time they are switched on.

