    there: an outline round every window with a thick accent ring round
    the one in use, and a blur that softens and dims every window but the
    one in use;
  * a KWin plugin for hot corners: an action for each outer corner of the
    screen, optionally only while a key is held, and the toast that says
    when a corner turned something on or off;
  * a KWin effect for touchpad gestures with three or four fingers, which
    follow the fingers: Task view, show the desktop, switch desktops, open
    Start's apps or notifications, and three-finger drag; it also minimises
    every window on Win+D and brings them back;
  * a KWin script that draws the taskbar underglow chosen in Settings, a
    glowing line along the top edge of the docked taskbar;
  * a wallpaper plugin for the Overclock theme's Warp picture that draws
    the W at its centre, lit by the underglow's flowing spectrum;
  * a "Wild OS" sign-in session in place of Plasma's own entries.
 .
